/target
/.venv
/benchmarks/generated_corpus/
/benchmarks/reports/
/benchmarks/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
# Both trees, not just the root: the Tauri client has its own `node_modules`
# and its own lockfile, and `/node_modules/` alone matches only the repo root.
/node_modules/
/gui/node_modules/
/docs/node_modules/
/docs/dist/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/target/
# Regression seeds are committed; everything else under `seeds/` is a fuzzer's
# working corpus and is not. A seed is the smallest input that a real bug was
# found by, so committing it means re-running a target after reverting a fix still
# fails, which is the only thing that proves the assertion has teeth.
#
# One level of `*`, not `**`: git cannot re-include anything inside an excluded
# directory, so `**` would exclude `seeds/graph_path_utils/` itself and the
# negations below would silently do nothing.
/fuzz/seeds/*
!/fuzz/seeds/graph_path_utils/
!/fuzz/seeds/resolve_focus_scope/
!/fuzz/seeds/README.md
# The Tauri client, excluded from the workspace for the reason its manifest gives:
# `tauri`, `wry` and WebKitGTK's system requirements must not reach
# `cargo test --workspace`. So it gets its own `target/` and its own lockfile,
# exactly as `fuzz/` does.
#
# The path is `src-tauri/target/`, not `target/`: the Tauri CLI builds from
# `src-tauri/`, and cargo resolves `target/` relative to the *manifest*, not to
# the repo root. The first version of this rule used `/gui/target/` and ignored
# nothing at all, which is how 9,000 object files ended up in a commit.
/gui/src-tauri/target/
/gui/dist/
# A real lockfile is committed for the front-end. `package-lock.json` is not
# optional here the way it is for `docs/`: the GUI is a product surface, and a
# build that resolves a different React minor version on a different machine is
# a build that cannot be reproduced.
# The graph corpus repositories are not ignored here on purpose. They live in a
# cache directory outside the tree -- see scripts/fetch_corpus.py -- because
# `graph` reads only the ignore patterns it is given and would analyse test data
# inside the repository as project code. CI overrides the location with
# SEPHERA_CORPUS_DIR, so this entry only covers a local run that does the same.
/.corpus/
**/*.snap
!crates/sephera_cli/tests/snapshots/*.snap
.astro
